site_src/subsystems/research/

# Handoff dashboard hub — derived timeline artifact (regenerated from git history
# by scripts/handoffs/build_handoff_timeline.py; never hand-authored or committed)
data/handoff_timeline.json
data/handoff_timeline.json.tmp.*

# Session bus: high-churn RUNTIME state, not version-controlled.
#
# Widened 2026-08-12 (guard-universe-and-worktree-isolation P1/2, C45
# precedent — the same untrack-and-gitignore ruling already applied to
# logs/agent_audit.log: tracked, append-only, written by every agent,
# conflicting on essentially every cross-branch merge with zero
# informational benefit from being in git history). The original narrower
# rule below kept agent-owned heartbeats/cursors/inbox/outbox tracked on the
# theory that task-boundary writes are infrequent enough to version; in
# practice all of it churns as uncommitted state continuously — five mains
# writing concurrently produced 89 git-tracked bus files in permanent merge
# contention, all night, across a single 21-conflict merge. Runtime
# coordination state wants exactly ONE live instance and zero versioning of
# its churn; the queue/routing PROTOCOL (BUS_PROTOCOL.md), the durable task
# briefs (tasks/*.md) and the operator trust surfaces (tokens/token-queue.md,
# tokens/unblock.md, tokens/unblock.pins.json) are unaffected and stay
# tracked — this block ignores instance state, not the contract.
#
# advisory.jsonl (+ rotated advisory_<n>.jsonl shards) grows ~1 record/agent/
# tick; the coordinator-daemon heartbeat rewrites every tick; inbox/outbox/
# cursors/heartbeats/claims are per-agent runtime files rewritten or appended
# on every bus interaction. M3/M4 evidence is cited as a summary artifact,
# never the raw log.
coordination/session-bus/advisory*.jsonl
# Daemon-owned per-tick state. `boundary_state.json` was listed alone; the other
# three are the same kind of file and were left untracked-but-not-ignored, which
# is the shape that rides into another agent's `git add -A` on a shared tree.
coordination/session-bus/boundary_state.json
coordination/session-bus/relay_state.json
coordination/session-bus/stuck_state.json
coordination/session-bus/scheduling_recommendation_state.json
coordination/session-bus/adapter-ledger.jsonl
coordination/session-bus/inbox/
coordination/session-bus/outbox/
coordination/session-bus/cursors/
coordination/session-bus/heartbeats/
coordination/session-bus/claims/
logs/bus_supervisor.out
logs/bus_supervisor.pid
logs/coordinator_daemon.log

# AutoPilot operator runtime snapshots and diagnostic payloads stay local.
# Human ratification receipts (`artifacts/operator/ratify_*.json`) remain tracked.
artifacts/operator/*.lock
artifacts/operator/autopilot_state.pre-*.json
artifacts/operator/instrument_eras.pre-*.yaml
artifacts/operator/*operational_diagnostic*.json
artifacts/operator/*operational_baseline_candidate*.json

# Vidya pilot (docs/design/vidya-pilot-spec.md §11.0)
# The ledger is the canonical record but is regenerable from its adapters and large (~7.7MB for a
# full intake ingest), so it is not committed. The CHECKPOINTS are — an externally held checkpoint
# is precisely what upgrades the ledger from tamper-evident to tamper-proof for prior history, and
# git is the external holder. Never add .vidya/checkpoints/ here.
.vidya/ledger.jsonl
.vidya/ledger.jsonl.repair
.vidya/state.sqlite
.vidya/projections/

# Generated handoff-index sidecars (A19). `scripts/handoffs/index_state.py` derives
# both of these from the index files and the handoffs themselves — they are a VIEW,
# never a source, and regenerating is a single command. Tracking them made every main
# that ran index_state.py collide with the other three on a file none of them authored,
# which is why index_state.py had to be restricted to one session. The dashboard already
# treats absence as "index_state.py has never run in this checkout" and degrades to
# "no graph" (dashboard/panels.py, absence_means), so untracking costs nothing there.
handoffs/active/.index-state.json
handoffs/active/.index-graph.json

# Linked git worktrees (29 of them, incl. inference's live campaign trees).
#
# THIS ENTRY DOES NOT PROTECT THEM. Measured 2026-08-12, not assumed:
#   git clean -nd    -> 0 entries          (ignored, so not a candidate)
#   git clean -ndx   -> "Would skip repository" x29  (git skips nested repos)
#   git clean -nffdx -> "Would remove worktrees/"    (BEFORE *and AFTER* this entry)
# `-x` re-includes ignored paths and `-ff` defeats the nested-repo skip, so the
# only thing standing between `git clean -ffdx` and 29 live worktrees is that
# nobody types the second `f`. Ignoring is for STATUS HYGIENE here — it removes
# 29 untracked lines from every `git status` — not for safety.
worktrees/

# Append-only audit trail written concurrently by every agent (C45). Tracked until
# 2026-08-12: it conflicted on essentially every cross-branch merge, because both
# sides always append at the tail so a textual merge cannot interleave them. Read via
# scripts/utils/agent_log_analyze.sh; nothing reads it out of git history.
logs/agent_audit.log

# wrap-up 2026-08-12: runtime logs and merge artifacts. Same reasoning as C45
# (agent_audit.log): append-only or tool-generated files that every agent touches are a
# permanent merge tax with no read-side value in git.
llama.log
main.log
cache/
logs/*.out
logs/*.stale_src
*.orig

# Bus runtime state untracked 2026-08-12 (operator-approved, Phase-0 batch):
# queue + tokens + session pointer are live churn; daemon rebuilds queue state
# from bus files (BUS_PROTOCOL rule 9); operator decisions live in artifacts/operator.
coordination/session-bus/queue.jsonl
coordination/session-bus/tokens/token-queue.md
coordination/session-bus/tokens/unblock.md
coordination/session-bus/tokens/unblock.pins.json
logs/.current_session
